---
title: Gruyere and Black Pepper Popovers
servings: 16
rating: 5
notes: Makes enough for 2 tall popover pans. Recipe can be halved.
source: https://www.tastingtable.com/688704/gruyere-and-black-pepper-popovers-recipe/
tags: Bread, Sides
---

Position a rack in the bottom third of the oven.
Place 2 popover pans in the oven.
Preheat the oven to 375˚ with pans inside.

In a small saucepan, warm the @whole milk{2%cups} over medium heat
until it is hot (about 125˚) but not boiling. Remove from the heat.

In a large bowl, whisk the @eggs{4}(large) with the @salt{1.5%tsp}
and @black pepper{1/2%tsp} until smooth.
Slowly whisk in the warm milk.

Add the @all-purpose flour{2%cups} and whisk until the batter is just combined.
(It may be slightly lumpy.)

Cut the @Gruyère cheese{3%oz} into 16 small cubes.

Remove the muffin pans from the oven.
Spray the pans generously with nonstick @cooking spray{}.
Pour about 1/3 cup of the batter into each of muffin cups.
Set a cube of the cheese on top of the batter in each cup.

Bake the popovers until puffed and deep golden brown, about ~{40%minutes}
(do not open the door or they may collapse).
Remove the popovers from the pans, sprinkle with extra grated @Gruyère cheese{1%oz} and serve immediately.
